WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:11.500
Ovulation is a part of the menstrual cycle
when the ovary releases a ripe egg, or ovum.

00:00:11.700 --> 00:00:14.400
Inside the ovary are hundreds 
of thousands of follicles.

00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:19.800
Each follicle is a hollow ball of cells 
with an immature egg in the center.

00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:22.500
The typical 28-day 
menstrual cycle

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:26.200
begins on the first day 
of menstrual bleeding.

00:00:26.200 --> 00:00:28.500
During the first 
7 days of the cycle,

00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:31.000
a few follicles begin 
to grow at the same time.

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:36.000
These maturing follicles secrete 
estrogen hormone into the blood stream

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:41.400
to prepare the lining 
of the uterus for pregnancy.

00:00:42.300 --> 00:00:45.500
Around Day 7, all of the 
follicles stop growing,

00:00:45.500 --> 00:00:49.000
and begin to degenerate, 
except for one.

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:52.000
This dominant follicle 
continues to grow

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:56.800
and nourishes the 
developing egg inside it.

00:00:56.800 --> 00:01:02.900
Around Day 12, the follicle secretes a large
amount of estrogen into the blood stream.

00:01:02.900 --> 00:01:07.300
When the estrogen reaches the hypothalamus
and the pituitary gland in the brain,

00:01:07.300 --> 00:01:10.000
the anterior, or front part,
of the pituitary gland

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:13.000
releases a huge surge 
of luteinizing hormone

00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:14.900
into the blood stream.

00:01:14.900 --> 00:01:18.100
Around day 14, 
luteinizing hormone

00:01:18.100 --> 00:01:21.000
causes the follicle 
to undergo a sudden growth spurt.

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:23.000
Right before ovulation,

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:26.500
the egg detaches from
the inside of the follicle.

00:01:26.500 --> 00:01:28.800
The bulging follicle 
releases chemicals,

00:01:28.800 --> 00:01:31.500
causing one of the 
two fallopian tubes

00:01:31.500 --> 00:01:39.200
to move in closer 
and surround the follicle.

00:01:39.200 --> 00:01:41.900
The follicle swells until  
it bursts open,

00:01:41.900 --> 00:01:44.900
ejecting the egg and 
fluid from the follicle

00:01:44.900 --> 00:01:48.000
into the abdominal cavity.

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:51.889
In response, the fimbriae, 
tiny projections

00:01:51.889 --> 00:01:54.000
at the end of 
the fallopian tube,

00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:57.700
sweep across the ovulation site 
and pick up the egg.

00:01:57.700 --> 00:02:01.000
Microscopic cilia 
on the fimbriae's surface

00:02:01.000 --> 00:02:04.000
transport the egg to 
the entrance of the fallopian tube.

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:06.800
Inside the walls of 
the fallopian tube,

00:02:06.800 --> 00:02:11.900
muscular contractions gently push 
the egg toward the uterus.

00:02:11.900 --> 00:02:16.500
After ovulation, the egg 
lives for 12-24 hours,

00:02:16.500 --> 00:02:19.000
so it must be fertilized 
by a sperm from the male

00:02:19.000 --> 00:02:22.200
during this time for a 
woman to become pregnant.

00:02:22.200 --> 00:02:25.200
If it is not fertilized, 
the egg dissolves away

00:02:25.200 --> 00:02:28.200
and is shed along with the 
uterine lining during menstruation.

